"Penny Wright","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10765","person_slug":"penny-wright","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Peter Whish-Wilson","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10780","person_slug":"peter-whish-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Rachel Siewert","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10584","person_slug":"rachel-siewert","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Richard Colbeck","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10131","person_slug":"richard-colbeck","vote":"no"},{"name":"Richard Di Natale","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10755","person_slug":"richard-di-natale","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Ricky Muir","party":"Australian Motoring Enthusiast Party","person_id":"tvfy_10834","person_slug":"ricky-muir","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Sam Dastyari","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10819","person_slug":"sam-dastyari","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ludlam","party":"Greens","person_id":"tvfy_10713","person_slug":"scott-ludlam","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Scott Ryan","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10715","person_slug":"scott-ryan","vote":"no"},{"name":"Stephen Conroy","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10142","person_slug":"stephen-conroy","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Stephen Parry","party":"PRES","person_id":"tvfy_10507","person_slug":"stephen-parry","vote":"no"},{"name":"Zed Seselja","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10822","person_slug":"zed-seselja","vote":"no"}],"name":"Business - Rearrangement - Give more precedence to motion to disallow","noes":30,"question":"The majority agreed that the [motion to disallow](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2014-11-19/15) the [Corporations Amendment (Streamlining Future of Financial Advice) Regulations 2014](http://www.comlaw.gov.au/Details/F2014L00891/Explanatory%20Statement/Text) should take precedence over [question time](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Question_time#Australia) and motions to take answers. This was an [amendment](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2014-11-19.28.1) moved by Liberal Senator [Ian Macdonald](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/ian_macdonald) \"to test how genuine the Labor Party and the Greens are on the particular urgency of this motion\". It amends a [precedence motion](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2014-11-19.27.1) moved by Labor Senator [Claire Moore](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/queensland/claire_moore), which called for the motion to disallow to be considered without significant delay. ### A rebellious senator Palmer United Party (PUP) Senator [Jacqui Lambie](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/tasmania/jacqui_lambie) [crossed the floor](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/help/faq#rebel) and voted 'aye' in this division. This rebellion happened on the same day that she was removed as deputy Senate leader and deputy whip of PUP for not attending three party meetings this week (see [ABC News](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2014-11-19/palmer-united-party-demotes-jacqui-lambie/5901950)). ### Background to the motion Labor Senator [Sam Dastyari](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/nsw/sam_dastyari) introduced the motion to disallow the Regulation and gave a good [explanation](http://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?gid=2014-11-19.102.9) of his reasons for doing so. ABC News also gave a useful [summary](http://www.abc.net.au/news/2014-11-19/palmers-relationship-with-liar-lambie-hits-new-low/5904170) of the background of this motion, particularly under the subheading 'Coalition of com","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-3588","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2014-11-19/5"}
